{"name":"Deep Cherrywood","hex":"#6b473d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deep","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extending, reaching or positioned far from a point of reference, especially downwards.\nExtending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively.","Extending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Far, especially far down through something or into something, physically or figuratively.","In a profound, not superficial, manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep"},{"term":"cherrywood","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hardwood obtained from a cherry tree, valued for use in furniture and other woodworking applications."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherrywood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cherrywood, Dublin","blocks":[{"text":"Cherrywood is a developing suburb of Dublin, Ireland, bordering Cabinteely, Loughlinstown and Rathmichael. It is located to the southeast of the city, in Dún Laoghaire–Rathdown. The development commenced on a greenfield site in 1998 and primarily comprises Cherrywood Business Park and new residential and retail development. Development of the suburb stalled following the economic downturn, but resumed in the late 2010s and remains in continuous state of development as of late 2024."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherrywood%2C_Dublin"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/05._Tully_Burial_Ground_%26_Lehaunstown_High_Crosses.jpg/500px-05._Tully_Burial_Ground_%26_Lehaunstown_High_Crosses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/05._Tully_Burial_Ground_%26_Lehaunstown_High_Crosses.jpg/1280px-05._Tully_Burial_Ground_%26_Lehaunstown_High_Crosses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont